From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:33:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: RSS on the non-DSA MAC of an
 MT7986

On the GL-MT6000 a WAN download on eth1 (no DSA, no special tag) never
left ring 0 with the RSS table on rings 1-3, while LAN (DSA) uploads
were spread. Leave the
CDMP special tag as upstream (netsys v1 only), which 990-04 had turned
on for every version, and set the RSS rings mode field to PSE instead of
ORing PSE into its auto-learn reset value.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
index dac0f95..85f17bd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -3463,9 +3463,12 @@ static int mtk_rss_init(struct mtk_eth *eth)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	if (RX_DESC_OFS(eth, 1) == sizeof(struct mtk_rx_dma)) {
-		/* Set RSS rings to PSE modes */
+		/* Set RSS rings to PSE modes: the two-bit mode field comes up
+		 * as 3 (auto-learn) on the MT7986, so clear it first
+		 */
 		for (i = 1; i <= MTK_HW_LRO_RING_NUM; i++) {
 			val = mtk_r32(eth, MTK_LRO_CTRL_DW2_CFG(i));
+			val &= ~MTK_RING_AUTO_LERAN_MODE;
 			val |= MTK_RING_PSE_MODE;
 			mtk_w32(eth, val, MTK_LRO_CTRL_DW2_CFG(i));
 		}
@@ -4708,11 +4711,17 @@ static int mtk_hw_init(struct mtk_eth *eth, bool reset)
 	val = mtk_r32(eth, MTK_CDMQ_IG_CTRL);
 	mtk_w32(eth, val | MTK_CDMQ_STAG_EN, MTK_CDMQ_IG_CTRL);
 
-	val = mtk_r32(eth, MTK_CDMP_IG_CTRL);
-	mtk_w32(eth, val | MTK_CDMP_STAG_EN, MTK_CDMP_IG_CTRL);
+	/* The special tag on CDMP is netsys v1's, as upstream. With it on, an
+	 * MT7986's RSS hashes the switch's (tagged) packets and sends every
+	 * packet of the untagged non-DSA MAC (eth1, the GL-MT6000's WAN) to
+	 * ring 0.
+	 */
+	if (mtk_is_netsys_v1(eth)) {
+		val = mtk_r32(eth, MTK_CDMP_IG_CTRL);
+		mtk_w32(eth, val | MTK_CDMP_STAG_EN, MTK_CDMP_IG_CTRL);
 
-	if (mtk_is_netsys_v1(eth))
 		mtk_w32(eth, 1, MTK_CDMP_EG_CTRL);
+	}
 
 	/* set interrupt delays based on current Net DIM sample */
 	mtk_dim_rx(&eth->rx_dim.work);
